  "section_notes": "The final package keeps strict S1 reporting (24h for all incidents, 48h customer notice) and a 55°C/5% S2 limit, but S2 enforcement is softened: above-limit models may continue sales during an unspecified time-limited remediation under regulator oversight rather than an automatic stop. S3 requires new-unit shut-off immediately and a 6-year retrofit deadline with an alternative if retrofit is impossible; S4 requires built-in suppression from 36 months; S5 imposes a mandatory recall at 8 incidents/100k with 48h notices, though it permits resumption after verified corrective action. The stated red lines on public disclosure, retrofit length, customer access to test results, and suppression timing are all nominally respected."
